idge and Tony steps in to help.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-01-18\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":14,\"name\":\"Skeletons\",\"overview\":\"A mugging triggers a woman's repressed mernosy of her brother's murder, which she witnessed as a child. The suspect, free for the past 35 years, is tracked to the unlikeliest of hiding places by Tony and a visiting friend, L.A. homicide detective Paulie Pentangeli.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-02-08\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":15,\"name\":\"The Wicked Flee\",\"overview\":\"After seeing his mother killed by a stranger, a boy withdraws deep into himself, prompting a sympathetic Tony to step up his efforts to catch the murderer.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-02-22\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":16,\"name\":\"True Believers\",\"overview\":\"The unwelcome appearance in Eastbridge of white supremacists leads to a murder, with the suspicion soon arising that one or more of Tony's associates may be implicated.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-02-29\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":17,\"name\":\"Officer April\",\"overview\":\"After he shoots a woman in a drunken domestic squabble, Officer Kelly becomes the victim of a terrorization campaign.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-03-07\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":18,\"name\":\"Sex, Lies, and Kerosene\",\"overview\":\"Tony and Paulie investigate a puzzling arson case in which the husband of a beautiful woman appears to have been murdered.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-03-21\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":19,\"name\":\"Judgement Day\",\"overview\":\"Tony winds up in one of his own jail cells when he runs afoul of an imperious judge who's hiding a fearsome secret.\",\"still\":null,\"rating\":0,\"voteCount\":0,\"airDate\":\"1992-04-04\",\"runtime\":60},{\"number\":20,\"name\":\"Shoot the Breeze\",\